domain AgencyWipCloseout:
  description "Preserve the current agency work without claiming implementation completion."
problem P1:
  |
    The owner requested a handoff, WIP commit and push, then an end to today's work.
evidence E1:
  |
    Local inspection identifies the existing compact-psyche-repair-integration
    worktree at 0754ca7 with agency code, tests, documents and Seal objects dirty.
    Its main credential-domain checkout is /home/katsumata-m/kshiai.
evidence E2:
  |
    The latest verification record reports 709 tests passed before a final prompt
    adjustment. Formal adr:check is absent. Seal registration and four stale
    references remain incomplete. The owner did not request completion of them.
premise P2:
  |
    Preserve incomplete state honestly. WIP synchronization is not acceptance,
    merge, deployment or permission for a paid provider call. Do not modify other
    worktrees or end a shared workday based solely on repository closeout.
premise I1:
  |
    Inference from E1 and E2: the matching worktree is the continuation location. A handoff must preserve
    pending verification and Seal work rather than manufacturing completed gates.
decision D1 based_on P1, E1, E2, P2, I1:
  |
    Prefer an explicit WIP handoff and commit on the existing branch over further
    implementation or leaving unsynchronized work. Verify remote state through
    the main secdat domain, inspect staged paths for scope and sensitive data,
    push only this branch without force, read back its SHA and local cleanliness,
    and finish this task. Leave shared work-time lifecycle unchanged because the
    requested effects are repository handoff, commit and push.
